WEBVTT

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:01.293
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.877
- Hi, Theresa.
- Hi, Marissa.

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:04.712
- Eddie.
- I'm looking for Theresa.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.629
- We're engaged.
- Engaged?

00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:09.798
- You look good.
- I'm Marissa's mother. You're a student.

00:00:09.965 --> 00:00:12.050
- You mean it's over?
- No, I'll see you tonight.

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:13.842
A friend's in trouble.
I want you to help him.

00:00:14.051 --> 00:00:15.135
Uncle Shaun.
In that room...

00:00:15.343 --> 00:00:17.761
...you accidentally stumbled
into were documents...

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.096
...containing information
valuable to Caleb.

00:00:20.305 --> 00:00:22.598
- Construction's a dirty business.
- My answer's no.

00:00:22.806 --> 00:00:24.516
And Kirsten? She's complicit in this.

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:26.142
- Do you love her?
- I don't know.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.476
Be ready to fight for her.

00:00:27.726 --> 00:00:29.394
- I don't want you to go.
- Why don't I want to go?

00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:33.730
- But what kind of kiss was it?
- I don't know.

00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:35.856
A kiss. My lips, Theresa's lips. A kiss.

00:00:36.065 --> 00:00:38.524
Lips. Now, that's interesting.
Was there tongue?

00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:40.526
- I'm not answering that.
- Why?

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.652
- You really want to know?
- No.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.529
But just tell me this:
What level of kiss are we talking?

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.822
Was it like a Christina-Madonna peck?

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.115
Or was it a Britney-Madonna
sort of smooch?

00:00:50.323 --> 00:00:53.826
Or was it like a full-on
Al and Tipper Gore lip-Iock?

00:00:54.034 --> 00:00:56.494
- It was just a kiss.
- Okay. So you guys a couple now?

00:00:56.702 --> 00:01:00.413
Is she staying here? If so, where's she
gonna live? How? What's her credit like?

00:01:00.622 --> 00:01:04.416
What sort of lease is she looking to sign?
Are we talking a year or month-to-month?

00:01:04.624 --> 00:01:06.917
- Or is she looking to buy?
- There's no lease, okay?

00:01:07.126 --> 00:01:09.085
So then what? She goes back?
What do you do?

00:01:09.294 --> 00:01:10.920
Commute back and forth from Chino?

00:01:11.086 --> 00:01:13.171
If you're commuting,
whose car you gonna take?

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.506
How you gonna pay for gas?
What freeway is your freeway of choice?

00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:20.676
You gonna take the 55 to the 5?
Or the 91 to the 71? If you take the 71...

00:01:21.009 --> 00:01:22.885
- Just, whoa.
- Okay. I'll just whoa.

00:01:23.052 --> 00:01:26.596
You guys kissed, and I think you should
have a plan, because it's a big deal.

00:01:26.805 --> 00:01:28.597
- You're making it a big deal.
- Really?

00:01:28.806 --> 00:01:30.348
I don't even know when
I'd see her again.

00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:32.642
- Hi.
- Theresa. Hey.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.810
Hey. We were just
discussing your plan.

00:01:35.018 --> 00:01:36.686
- What plan?
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:39.437
I had the morning off,
thought you'd need a ride to school.

00:01:39.646 --> 00:01:40.855
- Oh, yeah. Great.
- Yeah.

00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:43.607
- I hope it's okay, me stopping by.
- It's fine. Come on.

00:01:43.815 --> 00:01:46.275
- Yeah. Sure. Why wouldn't it be?
- Okay.

00:01:46.775 --> 00:01:49.610
- Marissa. Hello.
- Hey.

00:01:50.778 --> 00:01:54.905
- Theresa. Hi. I didn't think you'd be...
- Staying? Yeah, well...

00:01:56.281 --> 00:01:58.699
- What's up?
- I thought maybe you'd need a ride...

00:01:58.908 --> 00:02:00.200
...to school.
- Oh. Thanks.

00:02:00.617 --> 00:02:02.160
Cool.

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:10.290
Well, I can go with Marissa,
and Ryan and Theresa can go together.

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:14.543
- No. No, Seth, really. It's okay.
- It makes more sense if you take them.

00:02:14.751 --> 00:02:18.295
Why? Because we go to the same school?
Because I live here?

00:02:20.755 --> 00:02:23.965
I'll go with Marissa,
and Ryan and Theresa can go...

00:02:24.174 --> 00:02:26.092
Yeah. Sorry. You know what?

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.760
- I should have called first.
- I should've called too.

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:32.387
- I'll just see you guys at school.
- I shouldn't just stop by. I'm gonna go.

00:02:32.596 --> 00:02:35.139
- No, wait, wait. It's...
- Call me later.

00:02:36.431 --> 00:02:37.432
We're hitchhiking.

00:03:17.624 --> 00:03:20.000
- Morning, beautiful.
- Good morning.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.543
Marissa.

00:03:21.918 --> 00:03:24.295
Kirsten. Sandy.

00:03:25.254 --> 00:03:29.590
Well, you're not gonna believe who is
Riviera Magazine's Man of the Year.

00:03:29.798 --> 00:03:32.383
- Theresa.
- Mrs. Cohen. Mr. Cohen.

00:03:33.342 --> 00:03:37.011
Well, that's nice. I mean, she really
deserves the award. Good kid.

00:03:37.219 --> 00:03:39.012
It's my dad.

00:03:40.013 --> 00:03:42.348
My vote stays with Theresa.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.058
- Hi.
- Hey. Is it a good morning?

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:49.144
So, Ryan, a couple of your friends
stopped by briefly.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.770
- Yeah, we know. It was awkward.
- Is Theresa staying?

00:03:51.979 --> 00:03:54.522
- Yeah. Looks that way.
- I thought she was going home.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.315
No. Change of plans.

00:03:56.523 --> 00:03:58.483
It's amazing. His lips don't even move.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.359
- Well, how long is she staying?
- Well...

00:04:01.985 --> 00:04:03.528
You tell them.

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:08.280
- We're figuring it all out.
- Is she gonna, what, rent a place?

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:10.949
What kind of lease? Month-to-month?
Year? Can she buy?

00:04:11.199 --> 00:04:13.367
- What you gonna do?
- I'm this way for a reason.

00:04:13.575 --> 00:04:16.953
- She's catering a tennis tournament.
- Is she gonna get a job after that?

00:04:17.161 --> 00:04:20.496
- What about the guy she's engaged to?
- Is she going back to school?

00:04:21.372 --> 00:04:24.124
- School. Bye.
- Now you know why I do the talking.

00:04:24.332 --> 00:04:26.917
We're gonna need a ride,
by the way. Thanks.

00:04:27.126 --> 00:04:29.210
I'll take them.
It's on my way to the office.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:32.796
- So is my dad gonna be in a good mood?
- Well, he should be.

00:04:33.004 --> 00:04:35.839
- He's Man of the Year.
- I meant the case.

00:04:36.048 --> 00:04:38.800
- Are you gonna take it?
- I'm thinking about it.

00:04:39.008 --> 00:04:41.593
We're gonna host the reception here
for my dad's award.

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:44.637
And it would be nice if Uncle Shaun
could be here.

00:04:44.845 --> 00:04:47.221
Not if we have to pay for the bar tab.

00:04:47.847 --> 00:04:49.973
I'm thinking about it.

00:05:06.525 --> 00:05:08.151
Hey.

00:05:09.485 --> 00:05:10.945
Hey.

00:05:15.489 --> 00:05:17.490
Can I ask you something?

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:19.325
Yeah. Sure.

00:05:20.993 --> 00:05:25.787
When you and I broke up,
and I started dating Ryan...

00:05:26.621 --> 00:05:29.998
...was it hard for you to see us together?
- Yeah.

00:05:31.249 --> 00:05:34.418
But, hey, we wouldn't
have broken up if I hadn't...

00:05:35.543 --> 00:05:37.545
...deserved it.
- I guess now I know...

00:05:37.753 --> 00:05:39.421
...what it feels like, huh?

00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:41.797
To deserve it.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:56.056
The sooner you realize that it's never
gonna go back to the way it was...

00:05:56.848 --> 00:05:59.517
...the sooner you can move on.

00:06:03.686 --> 00:06:05.771
Okay. I'll see you guys later.

00:06:05.979 --> 00:06:09.898
- Hey, Ryan. I'm sorry about this morning.
- No, no. That's okay.

00:06:10.107 --> 00:06:14.860
- I didn't realize she was gonna be there.
- Yeah. There was a change of plans.

00:06:15.068 --> 00:06:16.527
How long is she staying for?

00:06:16.694 --> 00:06:19.696
No, she's gotta find a job, a place to live.

00:06:19.863 --> 00:06:22.614
- Minor details, huh?
- Yeah.

00:06:23.907 --> 00:06:26.367
Well, if you need any help...

00:06:26.617 --> 00:06:28.326
Thanks.

00:06:31.203 --> 00:06:33.871
- Check out Gramps. He looks angry.
- That's because he is.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.623
Why? He's on a magazine cover.

00:06:35.831 --> 00:06:38.208
Hard to believe that doesn't
leave him fulfilled.

00:06:38.416 --> 00:06:41.501
Totally. I know. I love the society page.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:44.545
It's like, suddenly, all of the people
we know are famous.

00:06:44.712 --> 00:06:47.547
- Diana Kahn totally got a chin implant.
- They have chin implants?

00:06:47.755 --> 00:06:50.215
My dad does them.
He says chins are the new nose.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.301
- So did Picasso.
- Really? What hospital does he work for?

00:06:56.302 --> 00:06:58.303
Kidding. I'm not that dumb. Just shallow.

00:06:58.887 --> 00:07:02.014
Is all this talk of Newport and
plastic surgery boring you, Anna?

00:07:02.223 --> 00:07:04.474
No. Actually, I'm savoring it.

00:07:04.682 --> 00:07:08.268
I won't be hearing it much longer.
I'm leaving.

00:07:08.476 --> 00:07:12.104
- You getting dessert?
- No. I'm going back to Pittsburgh.

00:07:12.312 --> 00:07:13.563
- What?
- I'm gonna go live...

00:07:13.771 --> 00:07:17.232
...with my aunt and uncle.
I've just kind of had enough of Newport...

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.442
...so I'm leaving.

00:07:23.944 --> 00:07:27.655
Park-ranger cadet?
Full-time position available.

00:07:28.072 --> 00:07:29.948
I wouldn't look good in the hat.

00:07:30.157 --> 00:07:32.658
You'd get to put out forest fires.

00:07:32.867 --> 00:07:35.285
Moving on.

00:07:36.911 --> 00:07:39.204
Classifieds are...

00:07:39.412 --> 00:07:41.539
Depressing?

00:07:42.706 --> 00:07:46.167
- We'll find something. We'll figure it out.
- I know.

00:07:47.251 --> 00:07:49.919
I'm glad you called me to come meet you.

00:07:50.461 --> 00:07:54.589
Who knew being unemployed
could be so much fun?

00:07:59.967 --> 00:08:01.968
I gotta get to class.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:16.978
- It will be okay.
- Okay.

00:08:33.363 --> 00:08:34.905
Kaitlin. Hi.

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:37.199
Hi, Luke. What's going on?

00:08:37.407 --> 00:08:41.368
Well, I just finished school for the day,
you know, which is always a good thing.

00:08:41.576 --> 00:08:44.328
I so know what you mean.

00:08:45.787 --> 00:08:48.914
- Luke. What are you doing here?
- We're talking, Mom.

00:08:49.581 --> 00:08:52.166
Go get ready.
Daddy's coming to take you to dinner.

00:08:52.416 --> 00:08:55.001
So I'll see you soon?

00:09:00.171 --> 00:09:01.964
Luke, you know not to
come to the house.

00:09:02.173 --> 00:09:04.341
- We meet at the motel.
- I just thought...

00:09:04.549 --> 00:09:06.550
...that you needed help
with your DSL.

00:09:06.759 --> 00:09:09.802
Luke, as much as I want
high-speed Internet access...

00:09:10.011 --> 00:09:13.179
...it's not worth Kaitlin
becoming suspicious.

00:09:16.223 --> 00:09:18.599
Hey, Jules. Luke.

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:21.643
Luke just came by
to defrag my hard drive.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.353
Okay.

00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.771
Hurry along, Luke. Make it quick.

00:09:31.774 --> 00:09:34.026
I'll make sure Kaitlin's ready.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:43.240
Hey, should I put another piece of
swordfish on for Theresa? Or Marissa?

00:09:43.573 --> 00:09:45.700
Or any other ladies you plan
on having over?

00:09:45.908 --> 00:09:50.286
- I was gonna go pick up Theresa, so...
- Done and done.

00:09:50.494 --> 00:09:53.163
So how's that going with you guys?

00:09:53.913 --> 00:09:56.081
Good. Just trying to figure it out.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:59.417
- "It" being?
- Pretty much everything.

00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:02.710
- You want to know what I think?
- You're gonna tell me either way.

00:10:02.919 --> 00:10:06.379
Like my own son.
You're in high school, she should be...

00:10:06.588 --> 00:10:10.423
...you're both in way over your heads.
She's got no real job, no place to live.

00:10:10.632 --> 00:10:12.758
- Don't ask if she can stay here.
- I wouldn't.

00:10:12.967 --> 00:10:16.427
Good. You have no idea what Kirsten did
the last time I floated such a concept.

00:10:16.636 --> 00:10:19.387
Theresa's got family in Chino.
She's got a life in Chino.

00:10:19.554 --> 00:10:22.139
Running away is not the answer.

00:10:22.556 --> 00:10:23.807
I know.

00:10:24.015 --> 00:10:26.725
- It's kind of crazy.
- No. It's sweet.

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:31.228
It's totally misguided,
but it's kind of charming.

00:10:31.437 --> 00:10:37.190
You gotta tell her. It's time she faced
the music. Or at least the fianc Á.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:41.151
And you're gonna do that thing with
the white lights in your back yard, right?

00:10:41.359 --> 00:10:45.404
- Of course, Dad.
- Good. I love the white lights.

00:10:45.612 --> 00:10:48.948
- And no cilantro. I hate cilantro.
- You're Man of the Year.

00:10:49.156 --> 00:10:51.741
I think they can make some food
without cilantro.

00:10:51.991 --> 00:10:53.575
I'll have to make a toast.

00:10:53.784 --> 00:10:56.077
You've got that '73 Dom
in your wine cellar, yes?

00:10:56.285 --> 00:10:58.495
I think you went through that
on your birthday.

00:10:58.996 --> 00:11:03.248
- Kirsten. Mr. Nichol.
- Why don't you call him Caleb.

00:11:07.001 --> 00:11:08.835
- Congrats on your award.
- Means nothing.

00:11:09.043 --> 00:11:11.503
They're lucky I agreed to pose
for their front cover.

00:11:11.712 --> 00:11:14.672
Use that in your speech.
Want me to set a place for Theresa?

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:18.216
- I'll get back to you on that one.
- I'm gonna go check on the Dom.

00:11:18.424 --> 00:11:22.802
- I was thinking chardonnay for dinner.
- No, get the pinot.

00:11:23.594 --> 00:11:26.429
Do what you like. It's your house.
I'm just making a salad.

00:11:26.596 --> 00:11:29.515
Man of the Year and still so modest.

00:11:29.681 --> 00:11:32.767
I'm so glad to see it
hasn't gone to your head, Cal.

00:11:32.933 --> 00:11:35.393
The case. Have you made your decision?

00:11:35.602 --> 00:11:40.605
I've decided what it'll take to make me
decide. You tell Kirsten everything.

00:11:41.189 --> 00:11:44.399
- She's better off not knowing.
- She's not. You are.

00:11:45.024 --> 00:11:47.651
She is already implicated,
without her knowledge.

00:11:47.818 --> 00:11:49.527
Then why worry her?

00:11:49.736 --> 00:11:52.737
- This may all go away, you know.
- It may not.

00:11:52.904 --> 00:11:54.780
I won't spend the next year
lying to her.

00:11:54.989 --> 00:11:57.741
So if you want my help,
you tell her everything.

00:12:06.329 --> 00:12:08.122
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:12:08.331 --> 00:12:10.874
- We should talk.
- I have news.

00:12:12.416 --> 00:12:13.959
You go first.

00:12:14.251 --> 00:12:16.044
I just got off the phone with Eddie.

00:12:16.461 --> 00:12:19.921
And I told him I'm not coming home
anytime soon.

00:12:20.505 --> 00:12:22.881
- You did?
- He didn't take it well.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:25.841
But now that I did it,
which I can't believe I did...

00:12:26.008 --> 00:12:30.094
...I feel so much more free or something.

00:12:30.845 --> 00:12:33.221
What did you want to talk about?

00:12:35.806 --> 00:12:37.932
How do you feel about swordfish?

00:12:47.105 --> 00:12:50.315
- So she's leaving.
- No, she's staying.

00:12:50.524 --> 00:12:51.899
What? When did you
talk to Anna?

00:12:52.108 --> 00:12:54.067
She told me she's going
back to Pittsburgh.

00:12:54.276 --> 00:12:58.904
- Anna's going back to Pittsburgh?
- Not anymore, according to you.

00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:02.614
- I'm totally confused.
- She, Anna, is leaving.

00:13:02.823 --> 00:13:04.866
She, Theresa, is staying.

00:13:05.074 --> 00:13:06.867
Right. Got it.

00:13:08.201 --> 00:13:11.829
- So she really is leaving.
- That sucks.

00:13:12.496 --> 00:13:15.247
Do you think it's because of me?

00:13:16.998 --> 00:13:19.417
I can't believe I caused a girl
to leave the state.

00:13:19.625 --> 00:13:22.919
- The county, maybe. Sure. Fine.
- You really think it's because of you?

00:13:23.336 --> 00:13:26.921
Well, I mean, we broke up, she went
back East, she had a great time...

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:28.923
...she comes back, only to see me...

00:13:29.131 --> 00:13:31.883
...standing on a coffee cart
declaring my love for Summer.

00:13:32.091 --> 00:13:34.509
Maybe she just doesn't feel
that comfortable here.

00:13:34.718 --> 00:13:38.345
I know. I get that. But if it is because
of me, maybe I can talk her out of it.

00:13:38.554 --> 00:13:40.555
Except I can't ask her
if it's because of me...

00:13:40.763 --> 00:13:42.598
...without sounding totally
self-absorbed.

00:13:42.806 --> 00:13:45.683
And I'm not self-absorbed, right, Ryan?
Me. Me.

00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:49.936
- Me.
- Sorry. Just thinking about Theresa.

00:13:51.186 --> 00:13:54.689
- She's staying. What am I gonna do?
- She's leaving. What am I gonna do?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.320
Kiki, thanks for meeting me.

00:14:04.528 --> 00:14:07.655
- Is everything okay?
- Why don't you have a seat.

00:14:13.867 --> 00:14:16.202
Is it Uncle Shaun?

00:14:18.037 --> 00:14:22.790
The hotel room that he accidentally
stumbled into the other day...

00:14:22.998 --> 00:14:25.833
- Joel McKuin was staying there.
- That's quite a coincidence.

00:14:26.042 --> 00:14:29.419
Joel McKuin is the leading lumber
supplier on the West Coast.

00:14:29.919 --> 00:14:32.421
Not such a coincidence.

00:14:32.796 --> 00:14:36.590
It's not the first time that he's
accidentally stumbled into a hotel room.

00:14:36.798 --> 00:14:38.758
It's just the first time he's got caught.

00:14:38.966 --> 00:14:40.926
I knew Uncle Shaun
was a tough negotiator.

00:14:41.134 --> 00:14:44.511
And, yeah, he sent extra-nice
Christmas presents to certain Teamsters.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:48.139
Breaking and entering? Theft? What else?

00:14:48.347 --> 00:14:51.474
Blackmail? Racketeering?

00:14:53.892 --> 00:14:56.144
- Is he going to jail?
- Not if Sandy can help it.

00:14:56.352 --> 00:14:59.854
Well, if he can't,
are they gonna go after you?

00:15:00.938 --> 00:15:03.482
I'm afraid it's not just me.

00:15:13.279 --> 00:15:14.739
Hey.

00:15:15.197 --> 00:15:18.366
- Catching up on Western civ?
- Yeah, Spanish Inquisition. Lot of fun.

00:15:18.574 --> 00:15:21.785
Tell me about it.
Could they give us any more reading?

00:15:22.035 --> 00:15:23.869
- Get up.
- Eddie. Eddie, what's going on?

00:15:24.078 --> 00:15:26.621
You know exactly what's going on.

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:29.623
- You sleep with her?
- No. No.

00:15:29.831 --> 00:15:32.375
No? Then why'd she call me
and say she's not coming back?

00:15:32.583 --> 00:15:34.960
- Why would she stay here?
- This isn't the right time.

00:15:35.168 --> 00:15:37.711
No, don't touch me.
After all I did for you growing up.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:39.462
The least you can do is
be honest with me.

00:15:39.629 --> 00:15:41.630
Now, you be a man, and you tell me.

00:15:41.839 --> 00:15:43.632
- Are you sleeping with her?
- No.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:48.426
Excuse me. This lounge is
for faculty and students only.

00:15:52.137 --> 00:15:54.347
I'm not letting her go.

00:16:09.106 --> 00:16:12.024
Anna. Hey.

00:16:12.191 --> 00:16:14.026
- Hi.
- This is nice weather we're having.

00:16:14.234 --> 00:16:16.402
- Yeah.
- Yeah. Oh, did you hear? The Lakers won.

00:16:16.611 --> 00:16:18.779
- Oh, did they?
- Yeah. Yeah, they did.

00:16:18.987 --> 00:16:22.114
There's something else I wanted
to talk to you about. What was it?

00:16:22.323 --> 00:16:24.366
That's it. You're leaving.

00:16:24.574 --> 00:16:27.451
- Why the hell are you leaving?
- You know, I'm late for class.

00:16:27.659 --> 00:16:30.244
- You got at least three minutes.
- It's too complicated.

00:16:30.453 --> 00:16:33.121
Why don't you start with one reason.
There's gotta be...

00:16:33.288 --> 00:16:36.540
...one main, overriding reason.
- Fine. Look, I miss the seasons.

00:16:36.748 --> 00:16:40.834
I miss fall foliage. I miss the snow.
I miss the first signs of spring.

00:16:41.043 --> 00:16:43.711
- You miss the seasons?
- Yeah, and...

00:16:44.545 --> 00:16:45.921
And?

00:16:46.129 --> 00:16:49.048
And my little dog, Swifty.
We left him with my aunt and uncle.

00:16:49.256 --> 00:16:53.384
And the Jimmy Stewart Museum.
And Peanut Butter Cup Pie at Dingbats.

00:16:53.550 --> 00:16:59.554
The vinyl selection at Record Village.
And Sundays, the SuperFlea Fleamarket.

00:16:59.971 --> 00:17:02.514
I guess I did get it
into three minutes, huh?

00:17:02.723 --> 00:17:06.934
So that's it? There's not, like,
one other reason?

00:17:07.142 --> 00:17:10.144
- Did I say Peanut Butter Cup Pies?
- Yeah.

00:17:10.478 --> 00:17:13.480
- Then, no.
- Good. Excellent.

00:17:15.439 --> 00:17:17.857
Tomorrow, we're having this thing
for my grandpa...

00:17:18.066 --> 00:17:20.150
- I leave tomorrow.
- Not without saying goodbye.

00:17:20.359 --> 00:17:21.943
- I'll come say goodbye.
- Okay.

00:17:31.866 --> 00:17:33.450
Is there anything I can do to help?

00:17:33.659 --> 00:17:34.951
- You, Theresa...?
- Yeah, sure.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.703
She needs a job and a place to live,
if you got anything.

00:17:37.912 --> 00:17:40.371
Does she need a friend?
I could help out there.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.081
Invite her to Caleb's party.
We'll all hang out.

00:17:43.457 --> 00:17:46.208
Why the hell would you want that?

00:17:48.627 --> 00:17:51.295
Look, I'm used to getting what I want.

00:17:51.462 --> 00:17:54.213
Which I know is not
the most attractive quality.

00:17:54.422 --> 00:17:56.548
But I also know I can't compete
with a girl...

00:17:56.757 --> 00:17:58.841
...you've known your whole life.

00:18:00.259 --> 00:18:03.302
Not after everything that's
just come between us.

00:18:05.929 --> 00:18:10.682
I don't think she has clothes,
a dress, for it.

00:18:13.726 --> 00:18:15.852
But thanks.

00:18:30.653 --> 00:18:32.195
Hey.

00:18:33.321 --> 00:18:36.657
- How was the rest of your day?
- I wanted to see how you were doing.

00:18:36.907 --> 00:18:39.909
After the Heights,
I knew that my dad wasn't aboveboard.

00:18:40.117 --> 00:18:43.703
But this is beyond anything
that I could have imagined.

00:18:43.869 --> 00:18:45.245
We're gonna figure this out.

00:18:45.454 --> 00:18:47.872
You better believe I'll do
all I can to protect you.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:51.708
No. I don't want you to.
I'm going to get outside counsel.

00:18:51.999 --> 00:18:54.584
I do not want you involved.

00:18:55.418 --> 00:18:59.296
When I asked for your help,
I had no idea what I was asking you for.

00:18:59.504 --> 00:19:02.548
- I know that.
- But this is my mistake, not yours.

00:19:02.756 --> 00:19:08.093
And I will not let you compromise
yourself, not even for me.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:10.094
I'm gonna call the caterers.

00:19:10.303 --> 00:19:14.347
Make sure that there's no cilantro
for the Man of the Year.

00:19:26.688 --> 00:19:28.689
She's lying. I know it.

00:19:28.898 --> 00:19:32.733
- What? Who?
- Anna.

00:19:32.942 --> 00:19:36.861
- You're thinking about Anna right now?
- I just...

00:19:37.069 --> 00:19:40.405
I just wish I could convince her
not to leave because of me.

00:19:40.613 --> 00:19:43.657
You think she's leaving
just because of you?

00:19:43.865 --> 00:19:45.700
It makes sense, doesn't it?

00:19:45.908 --> 00:19:48.243
Yeah. But even if I thought it,
I wouldn't say it.

00:19:48.702 --> 00:19:52.204
I mean, it's a little self-absorbed, Cohen.

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:57.874
- I just never wanted to hurt her feelings.
- Maybe she just doesn't like it here.

00:19:58.082 --> 00:20:00.542
I hear there are a few people who don't.

00:20:00.751 --> 00:20:04.128
It does rain sometimes in January.

00:20:11.341 --> 00:20:13.300
I'm kind of...

00:20:14.051 --> 00:20:16.594
I'm kind of hungry. You want to eat?

00:20:17.261 --> 00:20:18.804
Thanks.

00:20:27.101 --> 00:20:28.727
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:20:28.935 --> 00:20:31.770
Are you still good at foot massages?
I've been on my feet...

00:20:31.937 --> 00:20:35.189
- We gotta talk.
- So no foot massage?

00:20:35.397 --> 00:20:38.816
Listen. Listen, I don't know
what to do about us.

00:20:39.025 --> 00:20:42.402
I can't get you a job, a place to live.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.236
- I live in a pool house.
- Shut up.

00:20:44.403 --> 00:20:47.822
Shut the hell up.
I don't need you to take care of me.

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:50.032
- I can take care of myself.
- I know, I know.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:54.868
I am not one of these Newport chicks
that needs a trust fund to survive.

00:20:55.076 --> 00:21:00.038
But the fact that you thought
I needed you is really great.

00:21:00.413 --> 00:21:02.248
Sweet.

00:21:03.081 --> 00:21:04.791
Sexy.

00:21:09.252 --> 00:21:11.378
What about Eddie?

00:21:12.212 --> 00:21:15.506
I told Eddie that I can't
marry him right now.

00:21:15.714 --> 00:21:17.674
Just because you're okay with it
doesn't mean he is.

00:21:17.882 --> 00:21:21.051
I'm not okay with it,
I just know it's for the best.

00:21:21.718 --> 00:21:23.969
I'm here to be with you.

00:21:31.724 --> 00:21:33.267
Are we doing this?

00:21:33.475 --> 00:21:36.686
It's not like we haven't before.

00:22:39.392 --> 00:22:41.851
- What's the matter?
- It's not like home.

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:44.812
I got people that notice
if I don't get back.

00:22:45.020 --> 00:22:48.564
I had the day off. If you want to go
to the beach or to the pier tonight...

00:22:49.148 --> 00:22:50.940
- Actually, I have a thing.
- A thing?

00:22:51.149 --> 00:22:53.400
Kirsten's dad is being honored
by some magazine.

00:22:53.609 --> 00:22:56.736
They're having a cocktail party
at the Cohen house.

00:22:58.112 --> 00:22:59.654
You...

00:22:59.821 --> 00:23:01.489
You want to come?

00:23:03.448 --> 00:23:04.574
Do you want me to come?

00:23:04.782 --> 00:23:08.535
- I'm kind of getting the vibe that...
- No. Yeah. No.

00:23:08.743 --> 00:23:11.745
It's just, you know what these things
are like, these people...

00:23:11.912 --> 00:23:13.621
And it might be kind of weird.

00:23:13.788 --> 00:23:17.249
The girl who serves food at the party
is now a guest at the party.

00:23:17.457 --> 00:23:18.833
I wasn't saying that.

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:24.128
- I feel like you're not trying to invite me.
- No, I do. I am.

00:23:24.336 --> 00:23:26.421
I didn't think you'd want to go.

00:23:26.629 --> 00:23:28.547
I don't want to go.

00:23:28.756 --> 00:23:31.841
I want to make sure you're not
embarrassed to bring me to things.

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:33.509
I'm not.

00:23:33.676 --> 00:23:37.303
Good. I have nothing to wear anyway.

00:23:38.303 --> 00:23:42.431
But come over after,
and we can both wear nothing.

00:23:52.396 --> 00:23:56.106
Well, if you keep looking up like that,
all you're gonna see is a bad shot.

00:23:56.315 --> 00:23:58.983
Hey, Hodes. How are things
at the DA's office?

00:23:59.191 --> 00:24:03.944
Better since you left the PD's office.
My people seem to win a few more.

00:24:04.195 --> 00:24:08.572
That's why I left.
I started feeling bad for you.

00:24:08.781 --> 00:24:12.241
So why don't I think it's a
wild coincidence to see you here?

00:24:12.491 --> 00:24:15.910
You have trust issues.
That's why you've never been married.

00:24:16.119 --> 00:24:20.622
Well, saves me a phone call.
We have a deal to offer your client.

00:24:20.830 --> 00:24:22.206
Client?

00:24:22.414 --> 00:24:23.874
Shaughnessy.

00:24:24.082 --> 00:24:27.042
- He's not my client.
- That's not what he said.

00:24:27.251 --> 00:24:31.295
He's drunk most of the time. You can't
take anything he says very seriously.

00:24:31.503 --> 00:24:35.006
We're taking what we think
he has to say very seriously.

00:24:36.256 --> 00:24:38.591
Just out of curiosity...

00:24:39.925 --> 00:24:42.052
...what kind of deal
were you gonna offer him?

00:24:42.260 --> 00:24:45.679
- Curiosity?
- Yeah, mild.

00:24:45.929 --> 00:24:50.807
Okay, if he were to cooperate, let us
know who signs his marching orders...

00:24:51.016 --> 00:24:52.975
...we'd plead him down
to a lesser charge.

00:24:53.184 --> 00:24:56.602
Unless the plaintiff decides
to drop the charges.

00:24:56.811 --> 00:24:58.604
Then he would have no reason to talk.

00:24:58.854 --> 00:25:02.189
Except the plaintiff has no reason
to do that. Right?

00:25:04.149 --> 00:25:09.360
Let me tell you something, Sandy. The
Newport Group is Orange County's Enron.

00:25:09.569 --> 00:25:11.737
You make this just a little
difficult for me...

00:25:11.945 --> 00:25:14.072
...and I'll come down on you
as hard as I can.

00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.740
- This must be a reelection year.
- Oh, spare me.

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:20.951
You and I have been friends for years.
That's why Caleb Nichol hired you.

00:25:21.159 --> 00:25:24.620
It used to be, Sandy Cohen's moral
compass wouldn't point him anywhere...

00:25:24.828 --> 00:25:27.914
...except the direction of truth.
No matter who he took down.

00:25:28.122 --> 00:25:30.957
Spoken like a man
who's never been married.

00:25:31.291 --> 00:25:34.126
I just can't hit it any better than that.

00:25:35.627 --> 00:25:37.753
Good to see you again.

00:25:43.965 --> 00:25:45.800
- Hey, man, where you been?
- Theresa's.

00:25:46.008 --> 00:25:48.301
- Your parents say anything?
- No, I covered for you.

00:25:48.510 --> 00:25:51.262
You shouldn't do this.
You're sleeping there? That's serious.

00:25:51.470 --> 00:25:53.721
- I fell asleep.
- I heard about some scary guy...

00:25:53.930 --> 00:25:56.014
...that showed up at school.
Was it Eddie?

00:25:56.223 --> 00:25:57.515
- He came to talk.
- Yeah?

00:25:57.724 --> 00:26:00.309
About how it's getting serious
between you and Theresa?

00:26:00.517 --> 00:26:03.436
- You and Anna? You talk?
- Do not change the subject to me.

00:26:03.603 --> 00:26:05.729
I'm powerless not to talk
about it. I tried.

00:26:05.937 --> 00:26:08.064
She had a list of reasons
why she's leaving.

00:26:08.272 --> 00:26:09.982
- Didn't make the cut?
- She's lying.

00:26:10.148 --> 00:26:12.817
I want her to know that I'm sorry
I hurt her feelings.

00:26:12.983 --> 00:26:15.902
But she doesn't have to do this.
She shouldn't be doing this.

00:26:16.110 --> 00:26:19.404
- Then just tell her.
- Just tell her, huh?

00:26:19.613 --> 00:26:21.947
Simple. Honest.
No wonder I never considered it.

00:26:22.156 --> 00:26:25.741
Okay, fine. I'll tell her tonight.
Might have to have a little bubbly first.

00:26:25.950 --> 00:26:26.950
A little veritas in vino,
know what I mean?

00:26:27.159 --> 00:26:28.743
Hardly ever.

00:26:30.036 --> 00:26:31.703
Coming.

00:26:36.707 --> 00:26:39.375
Hey. Come in.

00:26:40.250 --> 00:26:43.878
- How are you?
- Good. What's going on?

00:26:44.086 --> 00:26:46.921
- Well, there's this party tonight, and...
- I heard.

00:26:47.463 --> 00:26:50.465
Yeah, well, I thought
maybe you'd want to go.

00:26:50.674 --> 00:26:53.884
I can't. I didn't really bring
any of my nice clothes with me.

00:26:54.426 --> 00:26:57.261
Well, I have some options.

00:27:08.685 --> 00:27:13.646
Hello? Hello? Hey, Joel.
Thanks for getting back to me.

00:27:14.439 --> 00:27:16.481
No, actually, now's a perfect time.

00:27:16.732 --> 00:27:21.026
- Come on. Smile for your father, Kiki.
- I'm smiling on the inside.

00:27:21.318 --> 00:27:22.777
Veritas in vino.

00:27:23.027 --> 00:27:24.945
Yeah. Then we have a deal?

00:27:25.154 --> 00:27:27.572
Why spend a lot of money when
you can make a lot?

00:27:27.780 --> 00:27:29.740
Yeah. Caleb'll be pleased.

00:27:29.948 --> 00:27:33.992
Yes, Mr. McKuin, I'm fully aware.
We do what we must.

00:27:40.872 --> 00:27:42.456
Theresa coming?

00:27:42.664 --> 00:27:44.582
Nope. Marissa?

00:27:44.791 --> 00:27:46.625
I doubt it.

00:27:48.043 --> 00:27:53.922
Look, I get why you're doing what
you're doing, but she does really love you.

00:27:54.172 --> 00:27:58.549
- I know. It's just...
- Yeah. The Oliver thing. I know.

00:27:58.758 --> 00:28:00.217
It was messed up.

00:28:00.426 --> 00:28:05.512
But, hey, she dated Luke for years.
You can't always trust her judgment.

00:28:06.554 --> 00:28:09.306
But she has a good heart.

00:28:16.102 --> 00:28:18.645
Not your typical back-yard barbecue.

00:28:18.937 --> 00:28:21.689
Yeah, well, they never are.

00:28:24.482 --> 00:28:25.942
You...

00:28:27.484 --> 00:28:29.235
I had some help.

00:28:33.071 --> 00:28:34.530
Coop.

00:28:35.573 --> 00:28:39.450
- That's a nice one, sir.
- Right here, please. Eyes right here.

00:28:39.658 --> 00:28:44.745
Come on, Seth. Get in the picture.
You are the future of the company.

00:28:44.953 --> 00:28:46.955
There's something to look forward to.

00:28:47.163 --> 00:28:50.165
You'll grow out of comic books
and grow into wanting to be rich.

00:28:50.415 --> 00:28:51.457
No, I won't.

00:28:57.294 --> 00:28:58.837
- Hey.
- Hi.

00:28:59.546 --> 00:29:02.298
I just came to say goodbye.
My plane's leaving soon.

00:29:02.506 --> 00:29:04.674
- You're really leaving.
- Yeah.

00:29:05.174 --> 00:29:09.135
Well, you might not believe this,
but I'm gonna miss you.

00:29:09.302 --> 00:29:11.553
What's more unbelievable
is that I'm gonna miss you.

00:29:11.762 --> 00:29:13.430
Pretty unbelievable.

00:29:13.638 --> 00:29:17.057
- Bye, Blanche.
- See you, Rose.

00:29:19.141 --> 00:29:23.269
Have you seen Molly Miller's boob job?
They're huge.

00:29:23.436 --> 00:29:26.354
Lois Robin's face-lift?

00:29:26.521 --> 00:29:30.107
Diane Kahn totally had chin implants.

00:29:30.315 --> 00:29:31.691
They have chin implants?

00:29:31.858 --> 00:29:34.443
Oh, yeah. Chins are the new nose.
Haven't you heard?

00:29:34.651 --> 00:29:38.153
- Hey, Anna. Theresa.
- Nice to meet you.

00:29:40.947 --> 00:29:43.198
Came to say goodbye to Seth?

00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:45.575
Yeah.

00:29:46.117 --> 00:29:48.493
Could you give him this?

00:29:50.453 --> 00:29:52.871
It's supposed to say everything
that I couldn't say.

00:29:53.079 --> 00:29:54.539
But now that I'm here,
I just...

00:29:54.705 --> 00:29:57.290
...can't say anything at all.
- Yeah. Yeah. Of course.

00:29:57.874 --> 00:30:00.167
See you, Ryan.

00:30:01.543 --> 00:30:03.878
Thanks for teaching me how to waltz.

00:30:04.086 --> 00:30:08.214
Have the best life. You deserve it.

00:30:10.215 --> 00:30:11.674
- Bye.
- Bye.

00:30:23.515 --> 00:30:26.100
You look so hot.

00:30:26.559 --> 00:30:28.768
Not here, Luke. Behave.

00:30:28.977 --> 00:30:31.645
I know. It's just...

00:30:33.438 --> 00:30:35.147
...your ass.

00:30:44.403 --> 00:30:48.364
We do all right.
Excuse me, guys. Thanks.

00:30:51.866 --> 00:30:55.285
I saw the DA today.
It didn't go what I would call "well."

00:30:55.493 --> 00:30:58.328
I thought he was your friend.
You made deals all the time.

00:30:58.495 --> 00:31:02.081
It's an election year. It seems you're
not too popular with the people.

00:31:02.289 --> 00:31:04.624
That the best you could do?
I need to make my toast.

00:31:04.832 --> 00:31:07.584
I'll make this go away,
but you'll have to give something up.

00:31:07.793 --> 00:31:12.504
Joel McKuin needs to be the chief supplier
for the next big Newport Group contract.

00:31:12.712 --> 00:31:16.048
You won't be buying wholesale,
but it'll work.

00:31:17.590 --> 00:31:21.510
- I knew I could rely on you.
- Not if you were Man of the Century.

00:31:21.718 --> 00:31:25.387
What's the matter, Sandy?
You cut deals for your clients all the time.

00:31:25.637 --> 00:31:30.223
Yeah, well, usually, they're the ones
that have broken the law, not me.

00:31:33.559 --> 00:31:37.269
Mr. Nichol, it's time for your speech.
Right this way.

00:31:43.774 --> 00:31:45.358
Ladies and gentlemen,
it is my pleasure...

00:31:45.566 --> 00:31:48.401
- Hey, Jules.
- James.

00:31:48.568 --> 00:31:52.154
Now, forgive me, this can't
possibly be happening, right?

00:31:52.362 --> 00:31:57.157
- I'm crazy to even think it, right?
- Think what?

00:31:57.365 --> 00:32:02.202
Okay, that's what I thought.
Because it would destroy Marissa.

00:32:04.120 --> 00:32:05.662
We know she's been through enough.

00:32:05.871 --> 00:32:09.498
Honestly, Jimmy, I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:32:09.706 --> 00:32:13.584
- Now, Caleb's speaking.
- It really is a tremendous honor.

00:32:13.792 --> 00:32:15.752
Few publications better represent...

00:32:15.960 --> 00:32:20.004
...this great county of ours
than Riviera Magazine.

00:32:31.262 --> 00:32:33.680
I'll be right back.
I'm gonna give Seth his letter.

00:32:33.888 --> 00:32:37.015
Okay. I'll be here,
trying to spot the chin implants.

00:32:38.099 --> 00:32:40.767
My story has its own cast of characters.

00:32:40.934 --> 00:32:44.978
One doesn't become Riviera Man
of the Year without some help.

00:32:45.187 --> 00:32:47.480
Where would I be without
my wonderful family?

00:32:47.688 --> 00:32:49.982
My beautiful daughter Kirsten,
and my favorite...

00:32:50.190 --> 00:32:54.651
Well, my only grandson, Seth.
Come join me.

00:32:56.736 --> 00:32:59.904
- What are you doing here?
- I just want to talk. Can't you listen?

00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:06.117
- Let's go somewhere and figure this out.
- I'm not going anywhere.

00:33:07.909 --> 00:33:11.412
Stay the hell away from me. You're lucky
I don't kick your ass right here.

00:33:11.620 --> 00:33:13.788
- Look, can we please just go?
- Let go!

00:33:21.960 --> 00:33:23.919
What the hell is going on?

00:33:32.216 --> 00:33:34.301
Why don't you leave
before the cops get here.

00:33:34.509 --> 00:33:35.969
- You're dead!
- Right now.

00:33:36.177 --> 00:33:40.096
Don't ever come home. You're dead.
You hear me? Get off me, man.

00:33:51.645 --> 00:33:55.606
Oh, that's gonna be quite a shiner.
But, hey, they look good on you.

00:33:55.814 --> 00:33:56.982
Yeah? Thanks.

00:33:57.190 --> 00:33:59.942
I'm so sorry. About everything.

00:34:00.109 --> 00:34:02.235
Oh, it's okay, sweetie. It's not your fault.

00:34:02.444 --> 00:34:07.071
Hey, I heard there was a rumble in the
bedroom. I'm gonna go break it up.

00:34:10.532 --> 00:34:12.075
You okay?

00:34:13.159 --> 00:34:16.202
- I can't believe Anna didn't show.
- Actually...

00:34:19.162 --> 00:34:21.997
- You're just giving me this now?
- I was a little distracted.

00:34:23.165 --> 00:34:26.000
The ink's all smudged.
I can't even read it.

00:34:29.335 --> 00:34:31.086
Is that a V or a Q?

00:34:32.337 --> 00:34:34.088
Okay, here, look. Right there.

00:34:34.297 --> 00:34:37.716
That says, "I love you." Then what
is that word? "Azerbaijan"? "Aztecs"?

00:34:37.924 --> 00:34:39.467
- Aspirin.
- It says "aspirin"?

00:34:39.633 --> 00:34:42.594
- You're giving me a headache.
- "Confucius"? What's this C-word?

00:34:42.760 --> 00:34:43.928
- Confusing?
- "Confusing"?

00:34:44.136 --> 00:34:47.221
No. You're confusing me.
What do you care what it says?

00:34:47.430 --> 00:34:50.265
Anna couldn't even say goodbye.
She's leaving because of me.

00:34:50.432 --> 00:34:52.558
- I don't want it to happen.
- What is going on?

00:34:52.808 --> 00:34:56.185
Last week, you're on a coffee cart
declaring your eternal love for me.

00:34:56.394 --> 00:34:59.479
Now you're all like,
"Anna's letter. I can't read it."

00:34:59.646 --> 00:35:04.190
This isn't like that, okay? She's just my
friend, and I don't want her to leave.

00:35:06.692 --> 00:35:08.485
Then go.

00:35:08.693 --> 00:35:10.611
Stop her.

00:35:15.114 --> 00:35:17.782
- So, what are you gonna do?
- I need to call Eddie.

00:35:17.991 --> 00:35:20.659
Try and straighten everything out.

00:35:20.826 --> 00:35:22.702
It's gonna be okay.

00:35:23.452 --> 00:35:27.247
I'm sorry to interrupt. I need you to drive
me to the airport. I gotta stop Anna.

00:35:27.455 --> 00:35:30.665
- You can't drive yourself?
- I've had three glasses of champagne.

00:35:30.874 --> 00:35:33.209
You know how it goes
straight to my head. Please.

00:35:33.417 --> 00:35:35.919
- You should go. He needs you.
- Thank you very much.

00:35:40.004 --> 00:35:42.756
You're gonna be at the motel
when I get back?

00:35:42.965 --> 00:35:45.091
I don't want you to be late.

00:35:54.972 --> 00:35:57.390
Hey, Juju.

00:35:59.809 --> 00:36:03.728
- I wondered if you'd ignore me all night.
- You seemed busy.

00:36:03.936 --> 00:36:05.771
- Congratulations.
- Thanks for coming.

00:36:05.979 --> 00:36:07.605
Can I drive you home?

00:36:08.356 --> 00:36:11.566
- I can walk down the driveway.
- Can I call you?

00:36:12.108 --> 00:36:15.151
Take you out on a real date?
Things have gotten a bit crazy.

00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:18.654
Now, I know I didn't appreciate you.
I want to.

00:36:19.196 --> 00:36:21.864
I want to make you feel appreciated.

00:36:22.323 --> 00:36:27.159
Plan the perfect date, run it by me.
We'll see.

00:36:38.082 --> 00:36:39.959
Come on, man. Her flight leaves soon.

00:36:40.209 --> 00:36:41.751
I'm doing 75 in a 65, all right?

00:36:41.960 --> 00:36:44.461
"I'm doing 75 in a..."
Everyone knows 80 is the new 75.

00:36:44.670 --> 00:36:47.463
- What? Who talks like that?
- What is up with this a.c.?

00:36:47.630 --> 00:36:49.840
My Jewfro is frizzing out.
I look like Screech.

00:36:50.048 --> 00:36:52.425
- The a.c.'s fine.
- What is this music?

00:36:52.758 --> 00:36:55.760
Do not insult Journey. All right?

00:37:01.764 --> 00:37:04.224
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:37:05.808 --> 00:37:07.518
How are you?

00:37:07.726 --> 00:37:12.479
Just embarrassed. I can't believe it,
this huge fight at a fancy party.

00:37:12.687 --> 00:37:15.564
Actually not the first time
that's happened.

00:37:16.565 --> 00:37:20.150
Here. I'm not gonna have time
to get it dry-cleaned before I go.

00:37:20.609 --> 00:37:22.152
Before you go?

00:37:22.652 --> 00:37:26.071
I've been fooling myself thinking
this was gonna be easy.

00:37:27.155 --> 00:37:29.990
I made a huge mess of everything, and...

00:37:30.198 --> 00:37:33.826
...I have this whole life to figure out.
And so does Ryan.

00:37:34.076 --> 00:37:38.287
So take care of him.

00:37:38.454 --> 00:37:40.705
I'll see you.

00:37:55.839 --> 00:37:59.675
I talked to my dad.
He told me what you did.

00:37:59.884 --> 00:38:02.844
Obstructed justice.
Tampered with a witness.

00:38:03.177 --> 00:38:04.887
So, what happens now?

00:38:05.095 --> 00:38:09.431
My guess is, not much. Since it's an
election year, the DA can't afford to lose.

00:38:09.806 --> 00:38:12.600
And without this star witness,
they don't really have a case.

00:38:12.892 --> 00:38:15.226
And if you're gonna go
after the king, Caleb...

00:38:15.435 --> 00:38:17.811
...then you had better know
you can kill the king.

00:38:18.020 --> 00:38:20.146
I told you I didn't want you
to get involved.

00:38:20.355 --> 00:38:24.190
- I do what's best for my family.
- I'd rather go to jail than be responsible...

00:38:24.399 --> 00:38:29.068
...for you being mixed up in this,
getting into bed with my father.

00:38:29.277 --> 00:38:34.530
I promise you, I'd rather send you to jail
than get into bed with your father.

00:38:43.911 --> 00:38:47.538
You do something like this,
there's no going back.

00:38:47.830 --> 00:38:51.499
Yeah. It's kind of like prom night.

00:38:51.666 --> 00:38:53.917
Believe me.

00:38:54.126 --> 00:38:57.211
If anybody's gonna be putting
you in handcuffs...

00:38:57.378 --> 00:39:00.046
...it's gonna be me.

00:39:25.270 --> 00:39:27.021
Anna!

00:39:27.814 --> 00:39:31.733
- Anna, wait.
- Seth? Hold on.

00:39:33.359 --> 00:39:35.568
Seth, what are you doing here?

00:39:35.777 --> 00:39:41.530
Okay. Maybe it's just the champagne
talking, but I'm just gonna say it. Okay?

00:39:42.239 --> 00:39:44.991
- Please do not leave because of me.
- What? What are you...?

00:39:45.199 --> 00:39:47.242
You love me. I read it. And I get it. Okay?

00:39:47.451 --> 00:39:51.662
And I'm so sorry if I did anything
to hurt your feelings. Or cause this.

00:39:51.829 --> 00:39:54.372
But I don't want you to leave.
Okay? None of us do.

00:39:54.580 --> 00:39:58.624
Seth, I love you as a friend.

00:39:59.625 --> 00:40:03.086
- What?
- God, I love you as a friend.

00:40:03.294 --> 00:40:05.629
That doesn't say "Azerbaijan"?

00:40:07.547 --> 00:40:14.009
Look, I think you're an amazing guy.
A little self-absorbed, maybe, but great.

00:40:14.384 --> 00:40:18.137
But, I mean, if there's one thing that
our relationship taught me, it's that...

00:40:18.345 --> 00:40:20.847
...we don't have a lot of chemistry.

00:40:21.097 --> 00:40:22.806
So you're not leaving because of me?

00:40:23.223 --> 00:40:25.641
I'm leaving because I need to leave.

00:40:25.850 --> 00:40:29.519
But who knows? Maybe one day,
we'll be perfect for each other.

00:40:30.311 --> 00:40:32.145
I don't know.

00:40:33.813 --> 00:40:36.857
I do know I have to go to Pittsburgh.

00:40:37.482 --> 00:40:43.069
I'm Ionely, Seth. I thought
I could make this my home, but I can't.

00:40:44.695 --> 00:40:47.071
Thanks for coming...

00:40:48.906 --> 00:40:50.991
...and saying goodbye.

00:41:09.669 --> 00:41:11.837
Anna, wait a second.

00:41:12.129 --> 00:41:15.047
What am I gonna do without you?
Who will I play Jenga with?

00:41:15.256 --> 00:41:18.549
You're so wise. All your sage wisdom.
What am I gonna do without that?

00:41:18.758 --> 00:41:20.384
Confidence, Cohen.

00:41:32.642 --> 00:41:33.809
Anna!

00:41:57.824 --> 00:42:00.117
I'll be right back.

00:42:23.131 --> 00:42:26.425
What if the girl I'm supposed to be with
just went back to Pittsburgh?

00:42:26.634 --> 00:42:28.635
What if she went back to Chino?

00:42:29.719 --> 00:42:31.887
Why would Anna go to Chino?

00:42:32.888 --> 00:42:36.181
- I'm kidding. Come on.
- Nice one.

00:42:36.390 --> 00:42:39.350
Well, at least we have each other.

00:42:39.934 --> 00:42:42.143
Actually, I have Summer now.

00:42:42.352 --> 00:42:45.937
But I'll put a little Seth-Ryan time
on the books.

00:42:46.146 --> 00:42:48.898
- That's quality time.
- Thanks, buddy.

00:42:49.106 --> 00:42:51.357
I could always hang out with Luke.

00:42:51.899 --> 00:42:54.443
What do you think he's doing right now?

00:42:57.069 --> 00:42:59.112
Discovering fire?

00:43:00.071 --> 00:43:02.198
Hunting and gathering?

00:43:03.073 --> 00:43:07.284
Shaving his chest with a Buck Knife?
You guys could do that together.
